## D4 Post-Camp Feedback

iOS is the source of truth — ported `CampFeedbackSurveyView`,
`CampFeedbackResultsView`, `FeedbackObserver`/`FeedbackService`, and the two
`CampingDetailView` entry points.

- **Model**: `CampFeedback` + `ProgramFeedback` + `CampFeedbackPayload`/
  `toCampFeedbackOrNull` already existed (A10 data-model pass). Reused as-is — no
  duplication.
- **Service** (`data/feedback/FeedbackService.kt`): interface + Firestore
  (`loadMyFeedback` own doc, `submitFeedback` hand-built payload `set(merge)` with
  `submittedAt`/`updatedAt` = serverTimestamp, `loadAllFeedback` ordered
  `submittedAt` desc, limit 500) + in-memory `FakeFeedbackService` (with a `peek`
  test hook) + Hilt binding. Collection `campings/{id}/feedback/{uid}`.
- **Survey** (`ui/feedback/CampFeedbackSurveyScreen.kt` +
  `FeedbackSurveyViewModel`): availability window mirrors iOS — opens on the camp
  `endDate`, closes 60 days later. States: Loading / Error / NotAvailable (with
  open date) / Expired / Submitted (thank-you) / Editing. Form: 1–5 star overall
  (required to submit), per-session star ratings + optional comment (meals
  excluded, seeded from the schedule), highlights / improvements, would-return +
  submit-anonymously toggles. Submit filters `rating > 0` sessions, trims text,
  writes one doc keyed by uid, then shows the thank-you state.
- **Results** (`ui/feedback/CampFeedbackResultsScreen.kt` +
  `FeedbackResultsViewModel`): gated `canManageAnyCamping` (else Restricted).
  Aggregates: average overall (half-up star fill + 1-decimal), responses count,
  would-return %, per-program averages (best-first), and the written-comment
  stream (anonymous responses show "Anonymous"). States: Loading / Restricted /
  Error / Empty / Loaded.
- **Camp detail** (`ui/camping/CampingDetailScreen.kt`): added the "Share your
  feedback" card (shown in the 60-day window to approved participants, leadership,
  or the editor) and wired the previously-dead `ManagementSection` to a working
  "Feedback Results" entry (gated `canManageAnyCamping && camp ended`). The stale
  lodging/venue-map placeholder buttons in that section were removed (lodging is
  reached from Resources; venue map lands in D5).
- **Navigation**: typed routes `AppRoute.CampFeedbackSurvey` /
  `CampFeedbackResults` (`campings/{id}/feedback-survey` and `.../feedback`), two
  `composable` destinations in `CampzoneNavigationShell`.
- **i18n**: feedback strings added to EN, FR, PT-BR (incl. a `feedback_results_
  rating_count` plural with `one`/`many`/`other` for fr/pt).

## Data contract

- Doc ID == submitting uid; `overallRating` coerced/clamped 1–5 (RBAC); wire keys
  `campingID`/`userID`/`displayName`/`overallRating`/`programFeedback[]`
  (`id`/`programTitle`/`rating`/`comment`)/`highlights`/`improvements`/
  `wouldReturn`/`isAnonymous`. `submittedAt` + `updatedAt` overridden to
  `serverTimestamp()` on every write; `isAnonymous` hides `displayName` in the
  results UI but it is still stored.

## Notes / deviations (iOS authoritative)

- Results UI gates on `canManageAnyCamping` (matching iOS) even though the
  deployed rules also permit reads for `canViewParticipantProfiles` — the UI is
  intentionally the stricter of the two.
- No notification dispatch on feedback submit (none in the iOS flow or the
  backend contract).
